      "message": "\u003e Any failure here would prevent Gerrit from starting, I believe.\n\n\u003e I think we should avoid it happening. Maybe we could just log it if the registration doesn\u0027t work.\n\nDone\n\n\u003e This looks hacky indeed: can you explain the overall design?\n\nMy current approach:\n- If we\u0027re on a replica, there is no UI to redirect admins too, so log/ping the BSL page once at startup.\n- If there is a UI, inject a new `WebLoginListener` so that when admins login we can apply the same logic we use for normal plugins.\n\nI\u0027m no Guice expert, so if there is a better way of handling this from a Guice perspective, I\u0027m all ears.",
